---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Packages — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">For Developers</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Packages</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                A package is a canonical file tree, not a blob of GUIDs.
                <code class="text-foreground">querial.package.yaml</code> must contain
                <code class="text-foreground">format: querial.package/v1</code>.
            </p>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>querial.package.yaml
connections/catalog.yaml
pipelines/
  &lt;pipeline.code&gt;/
    pipeline.yaml
    README.md                 # optional
    steps/*.sql
    migrations/*.sql</code></pre>

            <h2>Codes are identity</h2>
            <p>
                Import creates database GUIDs. Never put connection strings, passwords,
                tokens, or ciphertext in the package. <code class="text-foreground">connections/catalog.yaml</code>
                lists logical stubs: name, provider, description. Allowed providers in v1:
                postgresql, sqlserver, mysql. If a stub is unresolved at import, materialization
                is blocked and the connection wizard opens.
            </p>
            <p>
                Creating stubs during import is an operator/admin action. Developers may
                export and import with remap or require-existing resolutions; creating
                unresolved endpoints is not this role.
            </p>

            <h2>Edges and retry maps</h2>
            <p>
                In <code class="text-foreground">pipeline.yaml</code>, <code class="text-foreground">to</code>
                depends on <code class="text-foreground">from</code>. Additive
                <code class="text-foreground">retry</code> maps are allowed; omit means product
                defaults (<code class="text-foreground">retry_max_attempts = 1</code> is off).
                There is no format v2 bump for those fields.
            </p>

            <h2>Where import lands</h2>
            <p>
                Import always materializes into the <strong class="text-foreground">current project</strong>.
                It does not copy pipelines into another project. There is no cross-project
                sharing in v1 — copy means export then import.
            </p>

            <h2>Git</h2>
            <p>
                Packages are designed to live in ordinary Git. Publication from the product
                is optional. Core operation never requires a remote. Operators configure
                remotes; this role authors the tree.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
